{"duration_api_ms":48454,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2dbc14c5-a00b-4954-ac7a-1194e12e1651","total_cost_usd":0.9085934,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":87273,"cache_read_input_tokens":517867,"output_tokens":5341,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2570},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":87273,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":659,"cache_read_input_tokens":295719,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13702,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13702},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":5341,"cacheReadInputTokens":517867,"cacheCreationInputTokens":87273,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9085934,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2570,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `labels/coder-1.json`. It seats Erin Houchin at **rung 1** on `israel-military-aid`: \"Continue full military aid to Israel with no new conditions.\"\n\n**What the chair rests on.** She cosponsored H.R. 8369 (118th), the Israel Security Assistance Support Act, and voted Yea on its final passage (roll call 217). The House split on that vote, 224–187. The bill is about one thing, and its operative sections do the following:\n- No funds may be used \"to withhold, halt, reverse, or cancel the delivery of defense articles or defense services from the United States to Israel.\"\n- All defense articles and services expected in fiscal years 2024 and 2025 must be delivered promptly.\n\nI read that as full aid with no condition on delivery. Both H.R. 8369 pages go in `rests_on`. They are one instrument, so the tier will compute as `single-source`.\n\n**This is the call most likely to differ from the other coders.** The annex treats \"no new conditions\" as an absence clause. \"Silence is not a clause\" rules out reading a mere Yea on aid as rejecting conditions. I treated this bill as different because its text forbids the executive to withhold delivery. That is stronger than voting against a conditioning amendment. A stricter reading would make the row BLANK `direction-only`.\n\n**The other passages:**\n- **H.R. 8034 (Israel security supplemental):** she voted Yea (roll call 152, 366–58). I coded both the vote page and the bill text `direction-only`. The annex says a supplemental shows continued aid but does not separate rungs 1 and 2. It is not near-unanimous, since 58 of 424 voting members (about 14%) voted No.\n- **Her campaign issues page:** it is written in the third person (\"Erin stands firmly with Israel\"), so it fails attribution. It is also rhetorical and undated, so it supports nothing.\n\n`needs_source` is empty, and I listed no quotes because no first-person words were in the sources.","ttft_ms":26129,"type":"result","duration_ms":50389,"uuid":"e7678387-4504-4a44-9b64-60ff158e1525","ttft_stream_ms":1376,"time_to_request_ms":74,"first_content_frame_ms":1376,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
